  "learnIntro": "How to use the app, how to practise, and how to look after your voice.",
  "learnAppTitle": "Using the app",
  "learnAppSummary": "A short tour of each tab.",
  "learnApp1": "Home shows today's sessions, your streak, your next reminder and any questionnaire that is due.",
  "learnApp2": "Exercises lists what your therapist prescribed for today. Open an exercise to read its steps.",
  "learnApp3": "Tick one box for each session you finish. Mark a session only after you have done it. Your therapist sees the same record.",
  "learnApp4": "Record is for the voice recordings your therapist asks for: a baseline before you start, follow-ups during the study, and practice takes whenever you like.",
  "learnApp5": "Progress shows how many of your prescribed sessions you completed, by day or by week.",
  "learnApp6": "Profile is where you set reminder times and sign out.",
  "learnApp7": "Short questionnaires appear on Home when they are due. Each takes one to five minutes.",
  "learnPracticeTitle": "Practising at home",
  "learnPracticeSummary": "Why regular practice matters and how to fit it in.",
  "learnPractice1": "Short, regular practice helps more than one long session.",
  "learnPractice2": "Practise at the times your therapist set. If you have more than one session a day, spread them out.",
  "learnPractice3": "Keep the sound easy. Exercises should feel comfortable, never forced.",
  "learnPractice4": "Stop if an exercise hurts or makes your voice worse, and tell your therapist.",
  "learnPractice5": "If you miss a day, start again the next day. Do not double up to catch up.",
  "learnPracticeNote": "Your therapist's instructions always come first.",
  "learnVoiceCareTitle": "Caring for your voice",
  "learnVoiceCareSummary": "Everyday habits that protect your voice.",
  "learnVoiceCare1": "Drink water through the day, unless your doctor has told you to limit fluids.",
  "learnVoiceCare2": "Avoid shouting, screaming and talking over loud noise.",
  "learnVoiceCare3": "Rest your voice when it feels tired.",
  "learnVoiceCare4": "Swallow or take a sip of water instead of clearing your throat.",
  "learnVoiceCare5": "Whispering strains the voice too. Use a soft, easy voice instead.",
  "learnVoiceCare6": "Avoid smoking and smoky places.",
  "learnVoiceCare7": "Limit caffeine and alcohol, which can dry your throat.",
  "learnVoiceCareNote": "This is general advice. Where your therapist's advice differs, follow theirs.",
  "learnStudyTitle": "About this study",
  "learnStudySummary": "What the study is and what happens to your data.",
  "learnStudy1": "This study looks at whether an app helps people keep up their voice exercises at home for four weeks, alongside their usual voice therapy.",
  "learnStudy2": "The app keeps a record of the sessions you mark as done, when you use the app, your voice recordings and your questionnaire answers.",
  "learnStudy3": "Everything is stored encrypted on this phone. The app sends nothing over the internet.",
  "learnStudy4": "Your therapist and the research team see your records. Data used for analysis carries your participant code, never your name.",
  "learnStudy5": "Taking part is voluntary. You can stop at any time without it affecting your care. Tell your therapist if you want to withdraw.",
  "learnStudy6": "Your therapist gave you the full Participant Information Sheet. Ask them if anything is unclear.",
